# ESTATE DEFAULT: LF. Ruled 2026-09-08 and chosen from MEASUREMENT, not preference --
# the estate was already 410 pure-LF against 319 pure-CRLF, .ps1 alone was 92 LF to
# 13 CRLF, and mixed-ending files were burning real time on failed edit anchors.
# A file that is CRLF in one place and LF in another makes any multi-line anchor a
# coin flip, which is the defect canon already records and this line ends.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.ps1  text eol=lf
*.psm1 text eol=lf
*.psd1 text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf

# THE ONE DECLARED EXCEPTION IN THIS ESTATE: .vbs wrappers are launched by wscript,
# and the convention predates this rule (see the runners repo). Stated, not assumed.
*.vbs  text eol=crlf

# Binaries pass through byte-for-byte. An EOL rewrite inside one corrupts it, and
# for anything hashed it would also invalidate the hash for no reason.
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.7z   binary
*.ots  binary
*.docx binary
